    "details": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><strong>Tracks</strong></p>\n<ul dir=\"ltr\">\n<li><strong>Software:</strong> Web or mobile apps, AI-powered platforms, intelligent systems, automation and data-driven tools.</li>\n<li><strong>Hardware:</strong> IoT devices, embedded systems, robotics, sensor-based systems and assistive technologies.</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">Technology choice is unrestricted in both tracks. Teams may blend AI/ML, cloud, IoT and software as their solution needs.<br /><strong>PROBLEM STATEMENTS YET TO BE ANNOUNCED</strong></p>\n<p dir=\"ltr\"><strong>Format &amp; Process</strong></p>\n<ul dir=\"ltr\">\n<li><strong>Round 0 &ndash; Registration &amp; Idea Screening (Online):</strong> Teams submit their initial idea. Shortlisting is based on problem relevance, innovation, feasibility and impact.</li>\n<li><strong>Round 1 &ndash; Discover, Define, Design &amp; Build (Offline):</strong> Shortlisted teams receive problem statements on Day 1 and build a working prototype. Mid-event evaluation and shortlisting follow.</li>\n<li><strong>Final Round &ndash; Demo &amp; Jury Q&amp;A:</strong> Each team gets a 10-minute presentation with live demo, then a 4-minute jury Q&amp;A.</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"ltr\"><strong>Eligibility &amp; Rules</strong></p>\n<ul dir=\"ltr\">\n<li>Teams of upto 4 members.</li>\n<li>Solutions must be original and built during the hackathon.</li>\n<li>A working prototype is mandatory for the final evaluation. Concept-only submissions will not qualify.</li>\n<li>AI/ML must solve a clearly identified problem, not serve as a decorative add-on.</li>\n<li>Participants must follow event discipline and the organizers' decisions are final.</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"ltr\"><strong>Prizes &amp; Perks</strong></p>\n<ul dir=\"ltr\">\n<li>Prize pool of ₹1,20,000 across both tracks (Top 3 winners per track)</li>\n<li>Certificates for participants, finalists and winners</li>\n<li>Goodies, mentorship from industry professionals, and industry speaker sessions</li>\n<li>Meals and refreshments throughout the event</li>\n</ul>",
